            <ArticleTitle>Oligometastatic prostate cancer to the navicular bone: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">This case of oligometastatic prostate cancer to the foot highlights the importance of: 1) metastasis remaining high in the differential for unexplained malady, in the setting of a primary cancer, despite an atypical presentation, and 2) comparing sequential imaging studies to baseline images, especially when remote, because subtle findings can declare themselves over time.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
